From c889266d847bf9f466f8861ff0f8462dd738cf62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:34:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(log): do not panic the environment on EMFILE opening
 a log file

__log_name treated any open error other than ENOENT as fatal and
panicked the whole environment ("log file unreadable" / "log file open
failed" -> __env_panic, which aborts in diagnostic builds).  Out of file
descriptors (EMFILE/ENFILE) is a transient, process-local resource
shortage, not corruption and not a wrong-user mistake.  __os_open
already retries it three times before giving up; when it finally
surfaces, panicking takes down every thread and process sharing the
environment for a condition local to this process and this moment.

Return EMFILE/ENFILE to the caller (as the enclosing commit / log flush
error) so the application can free descriptors and retry.  The
environment stays usable.  Genuine "wrong user / corruption" opens
(any other non-ENOENT error) still panic as before.

Test: test/db/log_emfile_nopanic.c injects EMFILE on log-file opens
through db_env_set_func_open (no real descriptor exhaustion, so it does
not perturb the harness), forces a log roll, and checks the write
returns EMFILE and a subsequent read does not return DB_RUNRECOVERY (the
environment was not panicked).  Control: no injection.  The unpatched
library panics the environment (aborts, under DIAGNOSTIC); the patched
one survives.

Found by dbsql (SQLite ioerr / fd-exhaustion tests).
---
 src/log/log_put.c                 |  13 +++
 test/MANIFEST                     |   1 +
 test/db/log_emfile_nopanic.c      | 184 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/db/run_log_emfile_nopanic.sh |  92 +++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 290 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 test/db/log_emfile_nopanic.c
 create mode 100755 test/db/run_log_emfile_nopanic.sh

diff --git a/src/log/log_put.c b/src/log/log_put.c
index e8235ecca..5455de95e 100644
--- a/src/log/log_put.c
+++ b/src/log/log_put.c
@@ -1787,7 +1787,20 @@ __log_name(dblp, filenumber, namep, fhpp, flags)
 	 * If the open failed for reason other than the file
 	 * not being there, complain loudly, the wrong user
 	 * probably started up the application.
+	 *
+	 * Transient, process-local resource limits (out of file descriptors)
+	 * are not corruption and must not panic the whole environment: return
+	 * the error so the caller can close handles and retry.  Panicking here
+	 * on EMFILE/ENFILE would take down every thread and process sharing
+	 * the environment for a condition local to this process and this
+	 * moment.
 	 */
+	if (ret == EMFILE || ret == ENFILE) {
+		__db_err(env, ret, DB_STR_A("5316",
+		    "%s: log file open ran out of file descriptors", "%s"),
+		    *namep);
+		return (ret);
+	}
 	if (ret != ENOENT) {
 		__db_err(env, ret, DB_STR_A("2520",
 		    "%s: log file unreadable", "%s"), *namep);
diff --git a/test/MANIFEST b/test/MANIFEST
index bf473857b..6c3672c8a 100644
--- a/test/MANIFEST
+++ b/test/MANIFEST
@@ -468,6 +468,7 @@ db	run_upgrade
 db	run_lock_priority_nullderef
 db	run_txn_remevent_leak
